==English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{der|en|enm|hod}}, {{m|enm|had}}, {{m|enm|hed}}, from {{der|en|ang|hād||person, individual, character, individuality, degree, rank, order, office, holy office, condition, state, nature, character, form, manner, sex, race, family, tribe, choir}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*haiduz||appearance, kind}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*(s)kāi-||light, bright, shining}}. Cognate with {{cog|osx|hēd||condition, rank}}, {{cog|goh|heit||person, personality, sex, condition, quality, rank}}, {{cog|non|heiðr}} {{gloss|"honour, dignity"}} (whence {{cog|da|hæder||honour}}, {{cog|sv|heder||honour}}), {{cog|got|𐌷𐌰𐌹𐌳𐌿𐍃||way, manner}}. Same as {{l|en|-hood}}.
{{rfv-etym|en}}
